# Bravo Healthcare — Accuracy (mandatory)

## Residential

Whenever Bravo Residential appears, it is **COMING SOON** / being developed. Never imply it is operating, accepting residents, or has available beds.

Primary residential CTA: `Receive Program Updates`.

## Contact

```
Bravo Healthcare
1601 Industrial Blvd, Ste 3059
Sugar Land, Texas 77478
Email: admin@bravohcs.com
Office Hours: Monday–Friday, 9:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m.
```

Do not invent phone or fax numbers. Hide those fields until real numbers are supplied. Do not add extra locations.

Emergency notice (required, not the primary CTA): `For medical emergencies, call 911.` Website forms are not emergency channels.

## Insurance

Approved wording only:

> Please contact our office to verify current payer participation. Coverage, eligibility, authorization, and benefits must be verified before services begin. Acceptance of an insurance plan does not guarantee payment.

Do not display insurer logos. Do not claim Medicare, Medicaid, or private insurance acceptance.

## Testimonials and statistics

Never fabricate testimonials, names, star ratings, or Google reviews. Hide the testimonial section if data is empty.

Never fabricate counters (clients served, caregivers, years, satisfaction scores).

## Healthcare language

Do not automatically call Bravo licensed, certified, accredited, Medicare/Medicaid-certified, HIPAA-compliant, award-winning, or nationally recognized. Do not claim services will cure, guarantee recovery, prevent hospitalization, or guarantee independence.

Do not claim the website is HIPAA compliant. Do not collect PHI (SSN, diagnoses, medications, insurance IDs) on public marketing forms.

If requested content conflicts with approved source files, flag the conflict and keep the approved version unless explicitly told to update it.
